---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-navy">About CSCU</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-navy/80">
      CSCU is the Computer Science Course Union at UBC Okanagan: a department-backed
      hub for CS and Data Science students, run by students.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-navy">History</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80">
      For most of its history, CSCU has run on year-to-year momentum. Each year's
      exec team, and whether the union stayed active into the next, came down to
      whether students stepped up to run and how well that team delivered. That made
      CSCU resilient in strong years and quiet in slower ones, but it also meant
      continuity was never guaranteed.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80">
      BC Hacks grew out of that same student energy: CSCU's hackathon, prominent in
      some years and dormant in others depending on who was around to run it.
      Alongside it, Coding Club formed with a clearer, standing purpose: build a
      coding community through consistent events, and create something durable
      enough to keep supporting students well beyond any single exec team's term.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-navy">Where CSCU is headed</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80">
      CSCU is now being restructured as a department-backed initiative, in
      partnership with the UBC Okanagan Department of Computer Science, to become a
      one-stop hub for the program rather than something that rises and falls with
      any single year's exec team. That means carrying forward what Coding Club and
      CSCU's other initiatives were always aiming at: one CS community, with steadier
      opportunities for everyone in the program, in whatever form that takes for a
      given year, from hackathons to ongoing community events.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-navy/80">
      Part of that work is supporting the wider ecosystem of CS-related clubs, not
      just running events itself. See the homepage for more on how CSCU works with
      the department and other clubs.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-8 text-navy/80">
      See the <a href="/about/constitution" class="underline hover:text-orange">constitution</a>
      for how CSCU is governed, or <a href="/team" class="underline hover:text-orange">the team</a>
      page for who's currently running it.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
